# RSpec for changed files

When you change Ruby code under `apps/fintr-be` (`app/`, `lib/`, or `spec/`), run targeted specs before finishing:

```bash
cd apps/fintr-be && make mchanged-specs
```

This uses `bin/rspec-changed` to map each changed file to its spec and run only those examples.

- Use `RSPEC_CHANGED_BASE=main make mchanged-specs` when comparing against `main`
- A **pre-commit** hook runs the same script on commit when backend app/lib/spec files changed (`bin/setup-git-hooks` from repo root; hooks live in tracked `.githooks/`)
- See skill `rspec-changed` for full workflow and path mapping rules

Do not claim backend work is complete until `make mchanged-specs` passes (unless the user explicitly skips tests).
